            <ArticleTitle>[Vitiligo, hepato-splenomegaly, and goitre after working with paratertiary butylphenol (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2216, 2221-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In three men vitiligo-like skin changes, enlargement of liver and spleen and diffuse goitre (grade II) with increased TSH secretion developed within one to two years of their having started work in a factory producing paratertiary butylphenol. These observations also tend to confirm the often discussed pathogenetic connection between vitiligo and thyroid disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
